  "response_text": "Introducing a high priority system that always chooses the task with highest is not a good idea because it may lead to situations where tasks with a low priority number may never run. Tasks are created with the intention of it being used, thus, if an algorithm prevents certain tasks from every running due to there always being a higher priority task, then it may cause the system to either crash or lose some of its intended functionality.  This was why robin-round scheduling was utilized for this lab: it ensures that every task, even if it has minimal impact, equally has a chance to run, ensuring that no thread is ignored.\\n",
